---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro"; import FdeNav from "../../components/FdeNav.astro"; import {roleFamily} from "../../data/fde";
const questions=["What production artifact will I personally own?","How often do I write and review production code?","Who owns the outcome after the proof of concept?","How much time is discovery, building, rollout, and adoption?","Does field learning change the core product? How?","What travel, on-site, clearance, or support load exists?","How are success and seniority measured?"];
---
<Base title="FDE Role Decoder | FDE Career Atlas" description="Compare Forward Deployed Engineer with solutions, applied AI, software, and deployment roles—and learn how to decode a job description." pageSlug="fde-roles"><FdeNav/><div class="shell roles"><header><p class="eyebrow">ROLE DECODER</p><h1>Job descriptions tell the truth that titles cannot.</h1><p>Titles are reused inconsistently. Compare technical ownership, customer outcome ownership, specialization, and the artifact you are expected to ship.</p></header><section><h2>Directional role map</h2><p class="note">These are market patterns, not universal rules. Read each company's job description.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Direct code ownership</th><th>Customer ownership</th><th>Center of gravity</th></tr></thead><tbody>{roleFamily.map(r=><tr><th>{r.role}</th><td>{r.code}</td><td>{r.customer}</td><td>{r.center}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section><section class="decoder"><div><p class="eyebrow">EVALUATE THE ROLE</p><h2>Seven questions to ask the hiring team.</h2><p>A good interview works both ways. Replace vague claims about “impact” with concrete ownership boundaries.</p></div><ol>{questions.map((q,i)=><li><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,"0")}</span>{q}</li>)}</ol></section><section><p class="eyebrow">SENIORITY</p><h2>Scope grows in four directions.</h2><div class="seniority"><article><span>01</span><h3>System</h3><p>From implementing one integration to owning a multi-system production architecture.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Customer</h3><p>From scoped delivery to shaping ambiguous, consequential workflows with senior stakeholders.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Reuse</h3><p>From solving once to turning field patterns into platform primitives and product improvements.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Organization</h3><p>From individual delivery to sequencing teams, managing risk, and raising engineering quality.</p></article></div></section></div></Base>
<style>.roles{max-width:1100px}.roles header{padding:6rem 0}.roles header h1{font-size:clamp(3.2rem,6vw,6rem);max-width:13ch}.roles header>p:last-child,.note{color:var(--fg-muted);max-width:58ch}.roles section{padding:4rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}tbody th{font-family:var(--font-body);text-transform:none;font-size:.85rem;color:var(--fg)}.decoder{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.75fr 1.25fr;gap:5rem;background:#fff1e6;margin-inline:calc(50% - 50vw);padding-inline:max(var(--pad),calc((100vw - 1100px)/2 + var(--pad)))!important}.decoder ol{list-style:none;padding:0}.decoder li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.5rem 1fr;border-top:1px solid #e4c3ae;padding:.8rem 0;margin:0;font-weight:650}.decoder li span,.seniority article>span{font:500 .65rem var(--font-mono);color:var(--accent)}.seniority{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);border:1px solid var(--line)}.seniority article{padding:1rem;border-right:1px solid var(--line)}.seniority p{font-size:.75rem;color:var(--fg-muted)}@media(max-width:750px){.decoder{grid-template-columns:1fr}.seniority{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}</style>
